# Architecture Boundaries

Respect the repository's existing architecture.

Before introducing logic, determine which layer owns it.

Rules:

- GUI / TrackerState orchestrates and presents state.
- Application owns deterministic application behavior and contracts.
- Infrastructure owns provider/API implementation details.
- GUI must not become an alternate service/domain layer.
- Provider-specific implementation details must not leak unnecessarily into provider-neutral contracts.

Never create a second source of truth when an existing contract can be extended.

Distinguish explicitly between:

- live mutable provider state
- generation/session-owned state
- canonical frozen data
- specialized presentation projections

Never derive canonical membership from filtered presentation state.

Never let specialized projections mutate or redefine frozen generic state.

When state belongs to one search generation, all data displayed as belonging to that generation must come from the same ownership boundary.